module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Ring.FilteredColimits
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Filtered.Final
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.ConcreteCategory.Basic
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Presentable.Directed
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Module.DirectLimit.FinitePresentation

/-!
# Maps of finitely presented modules over a filtered colimit of rings

Let `G : K ⥤ CommRingCat` be a filtered diagram of commutative rings whose stages are all
algebras over a fixed ring `A`, compatibly with the transition maps, and let `d` be a colimit
cocone with apex `R`.  This file proves items (2) and (3) of [Stacks Project, Tag 05N7] in that
situation: an `R`-linear map between the base changes to `R` of two `A`-modules whose source is
finitely presented is the base change of an `S`-linear map between the base changes to some stage
`S`, and two `A`-linear maps out of a finite `A`-module whose base changes to `R` agree already
have equal base changes to some stage.

Item (1) of the same tag, for the same shape, is
`Stacks.ModuleDescent.exists_extendScalars_iso_of_isColimit` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.Algebra`.

Neither statement carries `@[stacks 05N7]`: the tag is already placed, on all three items, on
`Module.exists_finitePresentation_and_baseChange_eq_of_lift_bijective`
(`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Module/DirectLimit/FinitePresentation.lean`), from which the two results
here are derived.  They are a change of index shape — a filtered colimit cocone in place of a
directed system — not new coverage of the tag.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RingFilteredColimits.legAlgHom`: a leg of the cocone, as an `A`-algebra map.
* `Stacks.RingFilteredColimits.mapAlgHom`: a transition map of the diagram, as an `A`-algebra map.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.IsFiltered.exists_directed_final`: a filtered category has a directed partially
  ordered final model whose objects live in the universe generated by its own.
* `Stacks.RingFilteredColimits.exists_descend_rTensor`: **Tag 05N7 (2)** for a filtered colimit
  cocone of commutative rings rather than for a directed system.
* `Stacks.RingFilteredColimits.exists_baseChange_eq`: **Tag 05N7 (3)** in the same shape.

## Implementation notes

The two statements are obtained from the directed-system forms
`Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.statement_three` and
  `Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.statement_one`, whose hypothesis
`Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.IsModuleColimit` — that `R ⊗[A] P` is the colimit of the
  `S ⊗[A] P` — is supplied by
`Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FPModules.isModuleColimit`.  Those results are stated for a
*directed preorder*, so the filtered index category is first replaced by a directed partially
ordered final model: a final functor does not change the colimit, and
`CategoryTheory.IsFiltered.exists_directed` provides the model after `CategoryTheory.AsSmall` has
made the index category small.  The single lemma `key` below packages the resulting data together
with every hypothesis the two
`Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent` results need, so that each of them is a two-line
  consequence.

Both the joint surjectivity of the legs and the finite-stage detection of an element dying in the
colimit are read off the colimit cocone restricted to the directed model, through
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Concrete.isColimit_exists_rep` and
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Concrete.isColimit_exists_of_rep_eq`.  The second of these needs the
forgetful functor to preserve the colimit, which is why the index category is taken to be small
here, unlike in `...F3b.ModuleLimits.Algebra`, where joint surjectivity alone was needed and could
be proved through the universal property.  For the intended application that costs nothing: the
index category of a diagram of schemes `D : I ⥤ Scheme.{u}` with `I : Type u` may be replaced by
`CategoryTheory.Functor.FullImage D`, which is small whatever the index morphism universe was.

The `A`-algebra structures on the stages and on the apex are instance arguments, with their
compatibility with the transition maps and with the legs of the cocone as the hypotheses `ha` and
`haR`; that is the form in which the global sections of a diagram of affine schemes over a fixed
stage present themselves.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05N7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05N7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05LI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05LI)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace CategoryTheory.IsFiltered

/-- A filtered category has a directed partially ordered final model whose objects live in the
universe generated by its own objects and morphisms.  `CategoryTheory.IsFiltered.exists_directed`
says this for a small category; `CategoryTheory.AsSmall` removes that restriction. -/
theorem exists_directed_final (K : Type u) [Category.{u} K] [IsFiltered K] :
    ∃ (J : Type u) (_ : PartialOrder J) (_ : IsDirected J (· ≤ ·))
      (_ : Nonempty J) (F : J ⥤ K), F.Final := by
  let e : K ≌ AsSmall.{0} K := AsSmall.equiv
  have : IsFiltered (AsSmall.{0} K) := IsFiltered.of_equivalence e
  obtain ⟨J, _, _, _, F, _⟩ := IsFiltered.exists_directed (AsSmall.{0} K)
  exact ⟨J, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, F ⋙ e.inverse, inferInstance⟩

end CategoryTheory.IsFiltered

namespace Stacks.RingFilteredColimits

variable {K : Type u} [Category.{u} K] [IsFiltered K] {G : K ⥤ CommRingCat.{u}}
  {d : Cocone G} {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [∀ l, Algebra A (G.obj l)] [Algebra A d.pt]

variable (haR : ∀ (l : K) (x : A), d.ι.app l (algebraMap A (G.obj l) x) = algebraMap A d.pt x)

/-- The leg of the cocone at `l`, as an `A`-algebra map. -/
def legAlgHom (l : K) : G.obj l →ₐ[A] d.pt := { (d.ι.app l).hom with commutes' := haR l }

variable (ha : ∀ {l m : K} (e : l ⟶ m) (x : A),
    G.map e (algebraMap A (G.obj l) x) = algebraMap A (G.obj m) x)

/-- The transition map of the diagram along `e`, as an `A`-algebra map. -/
def mapAlgHom {l m : K} (e : l ⟶ m) : G.obj l →ₐ[A] G.obj m :=
  { (G.map e).hom with commutes' := ha e }

include ha in
/-- A directed partially ordered final model of the index category, together with every hypothesis
of `Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.statement_one` and
  `Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.statement_three` for the restricted system. -/
private theorem key (hd : IsColimit d) (P : Type*) [AddCommGroup P] [Module A P] :
    ∃ (J : Type u) (_ : PartialOrder J) (_ : IsDirected J (· ≤ ·)) (_ : Nonempty J)
      (GJ : J ⥤ K)
      (_ : ∀ j : J, Algebra (G.obj (GJ.obj j)) d.pt)
      (f : ∀ ⦃i j : J⦄, i ≤ j → (G.obj (GJ.obj i)) →ₐ[A] (G.obj (GJ.obj j)))
      (ψ : ∀ j : J, (G.obj (GJ.obj j)) →ₐ[A] d.pt)
      (_ : ∀ (j : J) (x : G.obj (GJ.obj j)), ψ j x = legAlgHom haR (GJ.obj j) x),
      Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.TransitionSystem f ∧
        Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.IsCoconeAlg f ψ ∧
        Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.IsModuleColimit f ψ P := by
  obtain ⟨J, _, _, _, GJ, _⟩ := IsFiltered.exists_directed_final K
  let alg : ∀ j : J, Algebra (G.obj (GJ.obj j)) d.pt :=
    fun j => (d.ι.app (GJ.obj j)).hom.toAlgebra
  let _ : ∀ j : J, IsScalarTower A (G.obj (GJ.obj j)) d.pt := fun j =>
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x => (haR (GJ.obj j) x).symm
  set f : ∀ i j : J, i ≤ j → (G.obj (GJ.obj i)) →ₐ[A] (G.obj (GJ.obj j)) :=
    fun i j h => mapAlgHom ha (GJ.map (homOfLE h)) with hfdef
  have hds : DirectedSystem (fun j : J => (G.obj (GJ.obj j) : Type u))
      (fun i j h => (f i j h : G.obj (GJ.obj i) → G.obj (GJ.obj j))) := by
    refine ⟨fun i x => ?_, fun {i j k} hij hjk x => ?_⟩
    · show G.map (GJ.map (homOfLE (le_refl i))) x = x
      rw [Subsingleton.elim (homOfLE (le_refl i)) (𝟙 i), GJ.map_id, G.map_id]; rfl
    · show G.map (GJ.map (homOfLE hjk)) (G.map (GJ.map (homOfLE hij)) x) = _
      rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← G.map_comp, ← GJ.map_comp]; rfl
  have hf : ∀ (i j : J) (h : i ≤ j) (x : G.obj (GJ.obj i)),
      algebraMap (G.obj (GJ.obj j)) d.pt (f i j h x) = algebraMap (G.obj (GJ.obj i)) d.pt x := by
    intro i j h x
    show d.ι.app (GJ.obj j) (G.map (GJ.map (homOfLE h)) x) = d.ι.app (GJ.obj i) x
    rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, d.w]
  have hdJ : IsColimit (d.whisker GJ) := (Functor.Final.isColimitWhiskerEquiv GJ d).symm hd
  have hsurj : ∀ r : d.pt, ∃ (j : J) (s : G.obj (GJ.obj j)),
      algebraMap (G.obj (GJ.obj j)) d.pt s = r := by
    intro r
    obtain ⟨j, y, hy⟩ := Concrete.isColimit_exists_rep (GJ ⋙ G) hdJ r
    exact ⟨j, y, hy⟩
  have hinj : ∀ (j : J) (s : G.obj (GJ.obj j)), algebraMap (G.obj (GJ.obj j)) d.pt s = 0 →
      ∃ (k : J) (hjk : j ≤ k), f j k hjk s = 0 := by
    intro j s hs
    have h0 : (d.whisker GJ).ι.app j s = (d.whisker GJ).ι.app j 0 := by
      show d.ι.app (GJ.obj j) s = d.ι.app (GJ.obj j) 0
      rw [map_zero]
      exact hs
    obtain ⟨k, g₁, g₂, hg⟩ := Concrete.isColimit_exists_of_rep_eq (GJ ⋙ G) hdJ s 0 h0
    refine ⟨k, leOfHom g₁, ?_⟩
    have hg₁ : homOfLE (leOfHom g₁) = g₁ := Subsingleton.elim _ _
    have hg' : G.map (GJ.map g₁) s = G.map (GJ.map g₂) (0 : G.obj (GJ.obj j)) := hg
    show G.map (GJ.map (homOfLE (leOfHom g₁))) s = 0
    rw [hg₁, hg', map_zero]
  exact ⟨J, ‹_›, ‹_›, ‹_›, GJ, alg, fun {i j} h => f i j h,
    fun j => IsScalarTower.toAlgHom A (G.obj (GJ.obj j)) d.pt, fun j x => rfl,
    ⟨fun i x => DirectedSystem.map_self' f x,
      fun _ _ _ hij hjk x => DirectedSystem.map_map' f hij hjk x⟩,
    fun {i j} hij x => hf i j hij x,
    Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FPModules.isModuleColimit f hf hsurj hinj P⟩

include ha in
/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 05N7 (2)** for a filtered colimit cocone of commutative rings.  An
`R`-linear map between the base changes to the apex `R` of two `A`-modules, the source finitely
presented, is the base change of an `S`-linear map between their base changes to some stage `S`
of the diagram. -/
theorem exists_descend_rTensor (hd : IsColimit d)
    (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [Module.FinitePresentation A M]
    (N : Type*) [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N]
    (u : d.pt ⊗[A] M →ₗ[d.pt] d.pt ⊗[A] N) :
    ∃ (l : K) (ul : G.obj l ⊗[A] M →ₗ[G.obj l] G.obj l ⊗[A] N),
      ∀ x : G.obj l ⊗[A] M,
        u (LinearMap.rTensor M (legAlgHom haR l).toLinearMap x)
          = LinearMap.rTensor N (legAlgHom haR l).toLinearMap (ul x) := by
  obtain ⟨J, _, _, _, GJ, alg, f, ψ, hψ, htrans, hcocone, hmc⟩ := key haR ha hd N
  obtain ⟨j, ul, hul⟩ :=
    Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.statement_three f ψ htrans hcocone hmc
      ‹Module.FinitePresentation A M› u
  have hψ' : ∀ j, ψ j = legAlgHom haR (GJ.obj j) := fun j => AlgHom.ext (hψ j)
  refine ⟨GJ.obj j, ul, fun x => ?_⟩
  simpa [Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.canonMod, hψ', LinearMap.rTensor] using
    LinearMap.congr_fun hul x

include haR ha in
/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 05N7 (3)** for a filtered colimit cocone of commutative rings.  Two
`A`-linear maps out of a finite `A`-module whose base changes to the apex agree already have equal
base changes to some stage of the diagram. -/
theorem exists_baseChange_eq (hd : IsColimit d)
    (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [Module.Finite A M]
    (N : Type*) [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N]
    (v w : M →ₗ[A] N) (h : v.baseChange d.pt = w.baseChange d.pt) :
    ∃ l : K, v.baseChange (G.obj l) = w.baseChange (G.obj l) := by
  obtain ⟨J, _, _, _, GJ, alg, f, ψ, hψ, htrans, hcocone, hmc⟩ := key haR ha hd N
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := Stacks.FinitePresentation.ColimitDescent.statement_one f ψ hmc ‹Module.Finite A
    M› v w h
  exact ⟨GJ.obj j, hj⟩

end Stacks.RingFilteredColimits

end
